<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pacific Ocean</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pacific</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pacific Ocean is the largest ocean on Earth, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> to the west and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> to the east. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> crossed it to establish the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila-galleon">Manila galleon</a> trade, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> expanded to its northern shores. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> held Pacific island colonies, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a> across it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean.jpg" alt="Pacific Ocean" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CIA World Factbook · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pacific_Ocean_-_en.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
